IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcin-common`

-- Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic): "NOTICE OF INDEXED BENEFIT LEVELS AND OTHER AMOUNTS IN
-- ACCORDANCE WITH DIVISION 1 OF PART 13", Victoria Government Gazette No. S 363 of 30 June 2026, pages 11-18 (deposited text
-- lines 389-733 of ../../registers/source-bundle/GG2026S363.txt). The notice's own heading misspells the Act
-- ("REHABILIATION", line 393).
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. Every row of the notice that pays or limits a benefit to an individual, in the notice's own words and
-- order of subject, each with both printed figures; and the arithmetic a row states of itself (a ceiling "less 80% of
-- worker's current weekly earnings"; a death lump sum "in the following shares ... Balance"). Who asks, and the date, are
-- left to the seat layers (wcin-seat.l4, the injured worker; wcin-seat-family.l4, the dependants and family of a worker who
-- dies).
--
-- Covered: ss 161(a)(ii), 161(b)(ii), 162(a)(ii), 162(b)(ii), 163(2)(b), 164(1)(c), 165(4)(a), 165(5)(b), 166(1)(d)
-- (weekly payments); s 153(5) with Schedule 2 items 1 and 10, s 544 with Schedule 2 item 11 (pre-injury average weekly
-- earnings); ss 236(1)-(6), 237(1), 237(2), 237AA(1), 237A(1), 240(9) (death); s 241(2)-(7) (dependants' weekly pensions);
-- s 243(1)(b) (provisional payments); ss 211(2)(b)-(f), 212(b)-(e), 213(1)(a)-(e), 214(1), 214A(a)-(e), 217(1), (2)
-- (non-economic loss); s 221 with the Schedule 4 table, every item, and s 221(4); s 224(1)(b), (d), (e), s 229(4)
-- (medical and like services); s 301(3), (4) (dispute costs); s 340(a), (b), s 366(2) (damages).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the employer, insurer and self-insurer rows (s 106(1) and (2), line 718; s 72(1)(c), line 693; s 225(2),
-- line 690; Schedule 6 clause 1(1), lines 708-709; Schedule 7 clause 3(1), line 711; s 388(5), line 716); the indexation
-- arithmetic itself (the figures are encoded as printed; the rounding rules are in the Act). The Act is not deposited, so
-- pre-injury average weekly earnings, the entitlement-period percentages and week counts, who is a dependant, the impairment
-- rating and the formulas that combine a row's amounts are not worked out here: they are inputs.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Gazette's PDF, not the published
-- Gazette. Victoria Government Gazette, published by IVE Group Limited with the authority of the Government Printer for the
-- State of Victoria. (c) State of Victoria 2026. "This publication is copyright. No part may be reproduced by any process
-- except in accordance with the provisions of the Copyright Act." Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026
-- (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 -- the indexed amounts from 1 July 2026`

§§ `WEEKLY PAYMENTS (AWE) -- ss 161-166`

-- Lines 496-530:
--   "Weekly payments in First Entitlement Period / Where worker has no current work capacity
--    161(a)(ii) Maximum weekly payment $2,930 $3,000 / Where worker has a current work capacity
--    161(b)(ii) Maximum weekly payments – less worker's current weekly earnings $2,930 $3,000
--    Weekly payments in Second Entitlement Period / Where worker has no current work capacity
--    162(a)(ii) Maximum weekly payment for claims $2,930 $3,000 / Where worker has a current work capacity
--    162(b)(ii) Maximum weekly payment – less 80% of worker's current weekly earnings $2,930 $3,000
--    Weekly payments after Second Entitlement Period / Where worker has no current work capacity
--    163(2)(b) Maximum weekly payment – less 80% of worker's current weekly earnings $2,930 $3,000
--    ... Where worker has a current work capacity ...
--    165(5)(b) Maximum weekly payment where an application under section 165(1) has been approved – less 80% of worker's
--    current weekly earnings $2,930 $3,000"
-- s 163(2)(b) is printed under "no current work capacity" but takes off 80% of current weekly earnings (NOTES.md finding 9).
-- A worker after the second entitlement period with a current work capacity and no approved s 165(1) application has no
-- row: `not covered`.
GIVEN `the period` IS AN `Entitlement period`
      `the worker has a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application under s 165(1) has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Ceiling row`
`the 2013 Act maximum weekly payment row for` `the period` `with capacity` `the worker has a current work capacity` `approved` `an application under s 165(1) has been approved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `the first entitlement period` THEN
        IF `the worker has a current work capacity`
        THEN `answered` (`the ceiling row` "s 161(b)(ii)" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `less` 1)
        ELSE `answered` (`the ceiling row` "s 161(a)(ii)" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `less` 0)
    WHEN `the second entitlement period` THEN
        IF `the worker has a current work capacity`
        THEN `answered` (`the ceiling row` "s 162(b)(ii)" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `less` 0.8)
        ELSE `answered` (`the ceiling row` "s 162(a)(ii)" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `less` 0)
    WHEN `after the second entitlement period` THEN
        IF (NOT `the worker has a current work capacity`)
        THEN `answered` (`the ceiling row` "s 163(2)(b)" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `less` 0.8)
        ELSE IF `an application under s 165(1) has been approved`
             THEN `answered` (`the ceiling row` "s 165(5)(b)" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `less` 0.8)
             ELSE `not covered` `the notice prints no maximum weekly payment for this entitlement period, work capacity and claim`

-- Lines 514-530: "164(1)(c) Minimum current weekly earnings $251 $257"; "165(4)(a) Minimum weekly earnings for approval of
-- an application for a worker who has returned to work $251 $257"; "166(1)(d) Minimum current weekly earnings for approval
-- of an application for a worker who has returned to work under section 165 $251 $257".
GIVEN `the row` IS A `Minimum earnings row`
GIVETH A `Printed pair`
`the 2013 Act minimum earnings for` `the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row`
    WHEN `continuing weekly payments for an incapacity arising from surgery (s 164(1)(c), or s 93CA(1)(c))` THEN `printed as` 251 `then` 257
    WHEN `approval of an application for a worker who has returned to work (s 165(4)(a), or s 93CD(4)(a))` THEN `printed as` 251 `then` 257
    WHEN `approval of an application for a worker who has returned to work under s 165 or s 93CD(4)(a) (s 166(1)(d), or s 93CDA(1)(d))` THEN `printed as` 251 `then` 257

§§ `PRE-INJURY AVERAGE WEEKLY EARNINGS (AWE) -- s 153(5), s 544 and Schedule 2`

-- Lines 719-733: "153(5) and Schedule 2 Item 1 Column 3 paragraph (c) Where no rate applicable $2,930 $3,000";
-- "153(5) and Schedule 2 Item 10 Column 3 paragraph (b) Deemed pre-injury average weekly earnings for a full-time student
-- at time of completion of course $2,930 $3,000"; "544 and Schedule 2 Item 11 Column 3 paragraph (b) Deemed
-- pre-injury-average weekly earnings for a full-time student at a primary or secondary school at time of completion of
-- secondary school $1,700 $1,740".
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Pre-injury earnings item`
GIVETH A `Printed pair`
`the 2013 Act Schedule 2 amount for` `the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `Schedule item 1, column 3, paragraph (c): where no rate is applicable` THEN `printed as` 2930 `then` 3000
    WHEN `Schedule item 10, column 3, paragraph (b): a full-time student at the time of completion of the course` THEN `printed as` 2930 `then` 3000
    WHEN `Schedule item 11, column 3, paragraph (b): a full-time student at a primary or secondary school at the time of completion of secondary school` THEN `printed as` 1700 `then` 1740

§§ `COMPENSATION FOR DEATH OF A WORKER (CPI) -- ss 236-240`

-- Lines 415-453:
--   "236(1) For a dependent partner of partners in equal shares $759,510 $783,000
--    236(2) For an orphan child or orphan children in equal shares $759,510 $783,000
--    236(3) For a dependent partner of partners where there is one and only one dependent child payable in the following
--           shares: total amount of $759,510 $783,000
--    236(3)(a) For the dependent child $75,940 $78,290
--    236(3)(b) To the dependent partner/partners in equal shares Balance Balance
--    236(4) For a dependent partner or partners where there is more than one dependent child but not more than 5 dependent
--           children payable in the following shares: total amount of $759,510 $783,000
--    236(4)(a) To each dependent child $37,990 $39,170
--    236(4)(b) To the dependent partner/partners in equal shares Balance Balance
--    236(5) For a dependent partner or partners where there are more than 5 dependent children payable in the following
--           shares: total amount of $759,510 $783,000
--    236(5)(a) To the dependent partner/partners in equal shares $569,650 $587,270
--    236(5)(b) To the dependent children in equal shares Balance Balance
--    236(6) Maximum lump sum for dependent children if no dependent partner $759,510 $783,000"
-- "partner of partners" is the notice's misprint for "partner or partners" (NOTES.md finding 5).
`the 2013 Act s 236(1) total`    MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 2013 Act s 236(2) total`    MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 2013 Act s 236(3) total`    MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 2013 Act s 236(3)(a) child` MEANS `printed as` 75940  `then` 78290
`the 2013 Act s 236(4) total`    MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 2013 Act s 236(4)(a) child` MEANS `printed as` 37990  `then` 39170
`the 2013 Act s 236(5) total`    MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 2013 Act s 236(5)(a) partners` MEANS `printed as` 569650 `then` 587270
`the 2013 Act s 236(6) maximum`  MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000

-- One dependant's share, as the rows state it. A family with no dependent partner whose children are not orphans has only
-- the s 236(6) maximum, not a share: `not covered`. Partially dependent partners and other dependants are not in the split
-- (ss 237(1), 237(2), 237AA(1) print maxima only).
GIVEN `the dependant` IS A `Dependant kind`
      `the number of dependent partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER
      `the dependent children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the 2013 Act share of the death lump sum of` `the dependant` `with partners` `the number of dependent partners` `children` `the number of dependent children` `orphans` `the dependent children are orphans` `in` `the column` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent partners`)
        OR (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent children`)
        OR (`the dependant is a partner` AND `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0)
        OR ((NOT `the dependant is a partner`) AND `the number of dependent children` EQUALS 0)
    THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
    ELSE IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0
         THEN IF `the dependent children are orphans`
              THEN `answered` (`amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(2) total` DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent children`)
              ELSE `not covered` `the notice prints no share of the lump sum for this family, only a maximum: the Act, not deposited, divides it`
         ELSE IF `the number of dependent children` EQUALS 0
              THEN `answered` (`amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(1) total` DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent partners`)
              ELSE IF `the number of dependent children` EQUALS 1
                   THEN IF `the dependant is a partner`
                        THEN `answered` ((`amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(3) total` MINUS `amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(3)(a) child`) DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent partners`)
                        ELSE `answered` (`amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(3)(a) child`)
                   ELSE IF `the number of dependent children` AT MOST 5
                        THEN IF `the dependant is a partner`
                             THEN `answered` ((`amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(4) total` MINUS (`the number of dependent children` TIMES `amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(4)(a) child`)) DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent partners`)
                             ELSE `answered` (`amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(4)(a) child`)
                        ELSE IF `the dependant is a partner`
                             THEN `answered` (`amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(5)(a) partners` DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent partners`)
                             ELSE `answered` ((`amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(5) total` MINUS `amount` `the 2013 Act s 236(5)(a) partners`) DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent children`)
    WHERE
        `amount` p MEANS `the amount in` `the column` `of` p
        `the dependant is a partner` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the dependant`
            WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a dependent child`   THEN FALSE

-- Lines 444-453: "237(1) Maximum lump sum for any one or more dependent children or dependent partners or partially
-- dependent partners $759,510 $783,000"; "237(2) Maximum lump sum for any other dependants if no dependent partner or
-- dependent child or partially dependent partner $759,510 $783,000"; "237AA(1) Maximum lump sum for other dependents $20,000
-- $20,620"; "237A(1) Compensation for close family members for grief or loss $10,000 $10,310"; "240(9) Maximum amount for
-- reimbursement of expenses incurred by non-dependent family members $45,300 $46,700". How s 237(2) and s 237AA(1) relate
-- is not said (NOTES.md finding 12).
`the 2013 Act s 237(1) maximum`   MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 2013 Act s 237(2) maximum`   MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 2013 Act s 237AA(1) maximum` MEANS `printed as` 20000  `then` 20620
`the 2013 Act s 237A(1) amount`   MEANS `printed as` 10000  `then` 10310
`the 2013 Act s 240(9) maximum`   MEANS `printed as` 45300  `then` 46700

§§ `WEEKLY PENSIONS FOR DEPENDENTS OF WORKER WHO DIES (AWE) -- s 241`

-- Lines 455-492 (each $2,930 $3,000 unless shown):
--   "During the first 13 weeks
--    241(2)(a)(ii) Maximum weekly pension for a dependent partner
--    241(3)(a)(ii) Maximum weekly pension for two or more dependent partners in equal shares
--    241(4)(a)(ii) Maximum weekly pension for one orphan child
--    241(5)(a)(ii) Maximum weekly pension for two or more orphan children in equal shares
--    After first 13 weeks until the end of three years
--    241(2)(b)(i) Maximum weekly pension for a dependent partner
--    241(2)(b)(ii) Weekly pension calculation for a dependent partner where there are not more than four dependent children
--                  who are entitled to a pension
--    241(2)(b)(iii) Weekly pension for a dependent partner where there are more than four dependent children who are
--                  entitled to a pension $1,470 $1,500
--    241(3)(b)(i) Maximum weekly pension for two or more dependent partners in equal shares
--    241(3)(b)(ii) Weekly pension calculation for two or more dependent partners, where there are not more than four
--                  dependent children
--    241(3)(b)(iii) Weekly pension for two or more dependent partners, where there are more than four dependent children
--                  $1,470 $1,500
--    After first 13 weeks until child ceases to be eligible
--    241(4)(b)(ii) Maximum weekly pension for one orphan child
--    241(5)(b)(ii) Maximum weekly pension for two or more orphan children in equal shares
--    241(6)(b) Weekly pension calculation for each dependent child where there are not more than four dependent children
--    241(7)(b) Weekly pension for dependent children where there are more than four dependent children $976 $1,500"
-- s 241(7)(b)'s "from" figure is not the "before" figure indexed (NOTES.md finding 2).
--
-- The MAXIMUM rows: one dependant's maximum is the printed figure, divided equally where the row says "in equal shares".
-- A dependent child who is not an orphan has no maximum row; a partner after the end of three years has no row.
GIVEN `the dependant` IS A `Dependant kind`
      `the number of dependent partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the dependent children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` IS A NUMBER
      `the period` IS A `Pension period`
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Pension row`
`the 2013 Act maximum weekly pension row for` `the dependant` `with partners` `the number of dependent partners` `orphans` `the dependent children are orphans` `children` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` `during` `the period` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent partners`)
        OR (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
    THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the dependant`
         WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN
             IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0
             THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
             ELSE CONSIDER `the period`
                  WHEN `during the first 13 weeks` THEN
                      IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 1
                      THEN `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(2)(a)(ii)" `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for a dependent partner" `prints` `the 3000 row` `shared by` 1)
                      ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(3)(a)(ii)" `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for two or more dependent partners in equal shares" `prints` `the 3000 row` `shared by` `the number of dependent partners`)
                  WHEN `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years` THEN
                      IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 1
                      THEN `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(2)(b)(i)" `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for a dependent partner" `prints` `the 3000 row` `shared by` 1)
                      ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(3)(b)(i)" `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for two or more dependent partners in equal shares" `prints` `the 3000 row` `shared by` `the number of dependent partners`)
                  WHEN `after the end of three years` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no weekly pension row for this dependant in this period`
         WHEN `a dependent child` THEN
             IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` EQUALS 0
             THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
             ELSE IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0 AND `the dependent children are orphans`
                  THEN CONSIDER `the period`
                       WHEN `during the first 13 weeks` THEN
                           IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` EQUALS 1
                           THEN `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(4)(a)(ii)" `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for one orphan child" `prints` `the 3000 row` `shared by` 1)
                           ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(5)(a)(ii)" `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for two or more orphan children in equal shares" `prints` `the 3000 row` `shared by` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
                       OTHERWISE
                           IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` EQUALS 1
                           THEN `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(4)(b)(ii)" `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for one orphan child" `prints` `the 3000 row` `shared by` 1)
                           ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(5)(b)(ii)" `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for two or more orphan children in equal shares" `prints` `the 3000 row` `shared by` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
                  ELSE CONSIDER `the period`
                       WHEN `during the first 13 weeks` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no weekly pension row for this dependant in this period`
                       OTHERWISE `not covered` `the notice prints only an amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation here, not a maximum`
    WHERE
        `the 3000 row` MEANS `printed as` 2930 `then` 3000

-- The CALCULATION rows: the amount the notice prints for the Act's weekly pension calculation (the calculation itself is in
-- the Act, not deposited). No such row during the first 13 weeks, or for a partner after the end of three years. The
-- s 241(6)(b) and (7)(b) rows speak of "each dependent child" and "dependent children" without excluding orphans, and are
-- read literally.
GIVEN `the dependant` IS A `Dependant kind`
      `the number of dependent partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` IS A NUMBER
      `the period` IS A `Pension period`
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Pension row`
`the 2013 Act weekly pension calculation row for` `the dependant` `with partners` `the number of dependent partners` `children` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` `during` `the period` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent partners`)
        OR (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
    THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the period`
         WHEN `during the first 13 weeks` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation for this dependant in this period`
         OTHERWISE
             CONSIDER `the dependant`
             WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN
                 IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0
                 THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
                 ELSE CONSIDER `the period`
                      WHEN `after the end of three years` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation for this dependant in this period`
                      OTHERWISE
                          IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 1
                          THEN IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` AT MOST 4
                               THEN `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(2)(b)(ii)" `reading` "Weekly pension calculation for a dependent partner where there are not more than four dependent children who are entitled to a pension" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `shared by` 1)
                               ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(2)(b)(iii)" `reading` "Weekly pension for a dependent partner where there are more than four dependent children who are entitled to a pension" `prints` (`printed as` 1470 `then` 1500) `shared by` 1)
                          ELSE IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` AT MOST 4
                               THEN `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(3)(b)(ii)" `reading` "Weekly pension calculation for two or more dependent partners, where there are not more than four dependent children" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `shared by` 1)
                               ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(3)(b)(iii)" `reading` "Weekly pension for two or more dependent partners, where there are more than four dependent children" `prints` (`printed as` 1470 `then` 1500) `shared by` 1)
             WHEN `a dependent child` THEN
                 IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` EQUALS 0
                 THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
                 ELSE IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` AT MOST 4
                      THEN `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(6)(b)" `reading` "Weekly pension calculation for each dependent child where there are not more than four dependent children" `prints` (`printed as` 2930 `then` 3000) `shared by` 1)
                      ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` "s 241(7)(b)" `reading` "Weekly pension for dependent children where there are more than four dependent children" `prints` (`printed as` 976 `then` 1500) `shared by` 1)

§§ `PROVISIONAL PAYMENTS (CPI) -- s 243(1)(b)`

-- Line 494: "243(1)(b) Maximum amount for medical and other costs $11,320 $11,670".
`the 2013 Act s 243(1)(b) maximum` MEANS `printed as` 11320 `then` 11670

§§ `COMPENSATION FOR NON-ECONOMIC LOSS (CPI) -- ss 211-217`

-- Lines 531-571. The rows of ss 211(2)(b)-(e)(i) and 212(b)-(d)(i) print two amounts each, the second on the next line,
-- without labels (NOTES.md finding 3). Every printed amount is kept, in order.
DECLARE `2013 Act impairment band` IS ONE OF
    `s 211(2)(b)(i): a modified whole person impairment of not less than 10% and less than 11%`
    `s 211(2)(b)(ii): a modified spinal impairment of not less than 10% and less than 11%`
    `s 211(2)(c)(i): an impairment benefit rating of not less than 10% and not more than 30%`
    `s 211(2)(c)(ii)(A) and (B): a spinal impairment of not less than 10% and less than 30%`
    `s 211(2)(d): an impairment benefit rating of more than 30% and not more than 70%`
    `s 211(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%`
    `s 211(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%`
    `s 212(b): a psychiatric impairment of 30%`
    `s 212(c): a psychiatric impairment of more than 30% and not more than 70%`
    `s 212(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`
    `s 212(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`

-- READING of which band a rating falls in. The notice's own descriptions are used, and the specific rows first: a
-- "modified" rating from 10% to less than 11% is in s 211(2)(b); a spinal rating from 10% to less than 30% is in
-- s 211(2)(c)(ii), whose two rows (A) and (B) print the same words and amounts (lines 542-547) and the same amounts as
-- s 211(2)(c)(i); every other rating takes the general rows. A "modified spinal impairment" is read as "a spinal
-- impairment" in s 211(2)(c)(ii): from 11% to less than 30% it takes (c)(ii), not (c)(i) (the amounts are the same, only
-- the provision differs; NOTES.md finding 3). A modified whole person impairment is not spinal and takes (c)(i). No row
-- covers a permanent impairment under 10% or a psychiatric impairment under 30%.
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Impairment kind`, `the description` IS A `Rating description`, `the rating` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `2013 Act impairment band`
`the 2013 Act impairment band for` `the kind` `described as` `the description` `rated at` `the rating` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a permanent impairment` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the rating` LESS THAN 10
            THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for an impairment rating in this band under the Act named`
            IF `the rating` LESS THAN 11 AND `is modified whole person`
            THEN `answered` `s 211(2)(b)(i): a modified whole person impairment of not less than 10% and less than 11%`
            IF `the rating` LESS THAN 11 AND `is modified spinal`
            THEN `answered` `s 211(2)(b)(ii): a modified spinal impairment of not less than 10% and less than 11%`
            IF `the rating` LESS THAN 30 AND `is spinal`
            THEN `answered` `s 211(2)(c)(ii)(A) and (B): a spinal impairment of not less than 10% and less than 30%`
            IF `the rating` AT MOST 30
            THEN `answered` `s 211(2)(c)(i): an impairment benefit rating of not less than 10% and not more than 30%`
            IF `the rating` AT MOST 70
            THEN `answered` `s 211(2)(d): an impairment benefit rating of more than 30% and not more than 70%`
            IF `the rating` AT MOST 80
            THEN `answered` `s 211(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%`
            OTHERWISE `answered` `s 211(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%`
    WHEN `a psychiatric impairment` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the rating` LESS THAN 30
            THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for an impairment rating in this band under the Act named`
            IF `the rating` EQUALS 30
            THEN `answered` `s 212(b): a psychiatric impairment of 30%`
            IF `the rating` AT MOST 70
            THEN `answered` `s 212(c): a psychiatric impairment of more than 30% and not more than 70%`
            IF `the rating` AT MOST 80
            THEN `answered` `s 212(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`
            OTHERWISE `answered` `s 212(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`
    WHERE
        `is modified whole person` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the description`
            WHEN `a modified whole person impairment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `is modified spinal` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the description`
            WHEN `a modified spinal impairment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `is spinal` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the description`
            WHEN `a spinal impairment`          THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a modified spinal impairment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Lines 534-571, every amount printed for the band (the s 211(2)(e)(ii) and s 212(d)(ii) maxima are separate rows, below).
GIVEN `the band` IS A `2013 Act impairment band`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Printed pair`
`the 2013 Act amounts printed for` `the band` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the band`
    WHEN `s 211(2)(b)(i): a modified whole person impairment of not less than 10% and less than 11%` THEN LIST (`printed as` 15940 `then` 16430), (`printed as` 13580 `then` 14000)
    WHEN `s 211(2)(b)(ii): a modified spinal impairment of not less than 10% and less than 11%`      THEN LIST (`printed as` 15940 `then` 16430), (`printed as` 13580 `then` 14000)
    WHEN `s 211(2)(c)(i): an impairment benefit rating of not less than 10% and not more than 30%`   THEN LIST (`printed as` 25730 `then` 26530), (`printed as` 3860 `then` 3980)
    WHEN `s 211(2)(c)(ii)(A) and (B): a spinal impairment of not less than 10% and less than 30%`     THEN LIST (`printed as` 25730 `then` 26530), (`printed as` 3860 `then` 3980)
    WHEN `s 211(2)(d): an impairment benefit rating of more than 30% and not more than 70%`          THEN LIST (`printed as` 102950 `then` 106130), (`printed as` 6440 `then` 6640)
    WHEN `s 211(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%`          THEN LIST (`printed as` 358420 `then` 369510), (`printed as` 40120 `then` 41360)
    WHEN `s 211(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%`                               THEN LIST (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000)
    WHEN `s 212(b): a psychiatric impairment of 30%`                                                THEN LIST (`printed as` 25730 `then` 26530), (`printed as` 3860 `then` 3980)
    WHEN `s 212(c): a psychiatric impairment of more than 30% and not more than 70%`                THEN LIST (`printed as` 102950 `then` 106130), (`printed as` 6440 `then` 6640)
    WHEN `s 212(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`                THEN LIST (`printed as` 358420 `then` 369510), (`printed as` 40120 `then` 41360)
    WHEN `s 212(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`                                      THEN LIST (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000)

GIVEN `the band` IS A `2013 Act impairment band`
GIVETH A STRING
`the 2013 Act provision for` `the band` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the band`
    WHEN `s 211(2)(b)(i): a modified whole person impairment of not less than 10% and less than 11%` THEN "s 211(2)(b)(i)"
    WHEN `s 211(2)(b)(ii): a modified spinal impairment of not less than 10% and less than 11%`      THEN "s 211(2)(b)(ii)"
    WHEN `s 211(2)(c)(i): an impairment benefit rating of not less than 10% and not more than 30%`   THEN "s 211(2)(c)(i)"
    WHEN `s 211(2)(c)(ii)(A) and (B): a spinal impairment of not less than 10% and less than 30%`     THEN "s 211(2)(c)(ii)(A) and (B)"
    WHEN `s 211(2)(d): an impairment benefit rating of more than 30% and not more than 70%`          THEN "s 211(2)(d)"
    WHEN `s 211(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%`          THEN "s 211(2)(e)(i)"
    WHEN `s 211(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%`                               THEN "s 211(2)(f)"
    WHEN `s 212(b): a psychiatric impairment of 30%`                                                THEN "s 212(b)"
    WHEN `s 212(c): a psychiatric impairment of more than 30% and not more than 70%`                THEN "s 212(c)"
    WHEN `s 212(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`                THEN "s 212(d)(i)"
    WHEN `s 212(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`                                      THEN "s 212(e)"

-- Lines 552-554 and 567-569: "211(2)(e)(ii) Maximum amount where the worker's impairment benefit rating is more than 70% and
-- not more than 80% $759,510 $783,000"; "212(d)(ii) Maximum amount where worker's degree of impairment is more than 70% and
-- not more than 80% $759,510 $783,000". No other band has a printed maximum.
GIVEN `the band` IS A `2013 Act impairment band`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Printed pair`
`the 2013 Act maximum printed for` `the band` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the band`
    WHEN `s 211(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%` THEN JUST (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000)
    WHEN `s 212(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`       THEN JUST (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the band` IS A `2013 Act impairment band`, `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH AN `Impairment figures`
`the 2013 Act impairment figures for` `the band` `in` `the column` MEANS
    `Impairment figures` WITH
        `provision` IS `the 2013 Act provision for` `the band`
        `amounts`   IS map (GIVEN p YIELD `the amount in` `the column` `of` p) (`the 2013 Act amounts printed for` `the band`)

-- The lump sum after the notice's maximum. A band above 80% prints one amount, which is the answer. The band above 70% and
-- not above 80% has a printed maximum: the answer is the amount the Act's formula gives (an input, since the formula is not
-- deposited) or the maximum, whichever is less. Every other band prints amounts the Act's formula combines and no maximum:
-- `not covered`.
GIVEN `the band` IS A `2013 Act impairment band`, `the column` IS A `Notice column`, `the formula amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the 2013 Act non-economic loss lump sum for` `the band` `in` `the column` `on a formula amount of` `the formula amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the band`
    WHEN `s 211(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%` THEN `answered` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000))
    WHEN `s 212(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`        THEN `answered` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000))
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the 2013 Act maximum printed for` `the band`
        WHEN JUST `the maximum` THEN `answered` (min `the formula amount` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` `the maximum`))
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no maximum for this impairment band, and the Act's formula that combines its amounts is not deposited`

-- Lines 572-586 and 589-601: further injury (industrial deafness) under s 213(1) and further impairment (EPD) under s 214A,
-- by 'T' and 'P', which the notice does not define. Rows (a) and (d) print two amounts, rows (c) three, rows (b) and (e)
-- one (NOTES.md finding 3). No row covers a 'T' under 10%.
DECLARE `2013 Act further impairment provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 213(1): further injury, industrial deafness`
    `s 214A: further impairment (EPD)`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `2013 Act further impairment provision`, `T` IS A NUMBER, `P` IS A NUMBER, `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Impairment figures`
`the 2013 Act further impairment figures for` `the provision` `with T` `T` `and P` `P` `in` `the column` MEANS
    IF `T` LESS THAN 10 OR `P` LESS THAN 0
    THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for an impairment rating in this band under the Act named`
    ELSE IF `T` AT MOST 30
         THEN IF `P` LESS THAN 10
              THEN `answered` (`figures` "(a)" (LIST `a 3980`, `a 2620`))
              ELSE `answered` (`figures` "(b)" (LIST `a 3980`))
         ELSE IF `P` LESS THAN 10
              THEN `answered` (`figures` "(c)" (LIST `a 6640`, `a 3980`, `a 2620`))
              ELSE IF `P` LESS THAN 30
                   THEN `answered` (`figures` "(d)" (LIST `a 6640`, `a 3980`))
                   ELSE `answered` (`figures` "(e)" (LIST `a 6640`))
    WHERE
        `a 3980` MEANS `printed as` 3860 `then` 3980
        `a 2620` MEANS `printed as` 2540 `then` 2620
        `a 6640` MEANS `printed as` 6440 `then` 6640
        `figures` paragraph pairs MEANS
            `Impairment figures` WITH
                `provision` IS CONCAT `the section`, paragraph
                `amounts`   IS map (GIVEN p YIELD `the amount in` `the column` `of` p) pairs
        `the section` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the provision`
            WHEN `s 213(1): further injury, industrial deafness` THEN "s 213(1)"
            WHEN `s 214A: further impairment (EPD)`              THEN "s 214A"

-- Line 588: "214(1) Loss of a foetus or loss of more than one foetus $92,570 $95,430".
`the 2013 Act s 214(1) amount` MEANS `printed as` 92570 `then` 95430

-- Lines 602-606: "217(1) Maximum amount of compensation for more than one injury suffered on the same occasion $759,510
-- $783,000"; "217(2) Maximum amount of compensation for more than one kind of non-economic loss for the same injury
-- $759,510 $783,000".
GIVEN `the limit` IS A `Non-economic loss limit`
GIVETH A `Printed pair`
`the 2013 Act s 217 maximum for` `the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `more than one injury suffered on the same occasion`          THEN `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
    WHEN `more than one kind of non-economic loss for the same injury` THEN `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000

-- The s 217 maximum applied to a total: the total (worked out under the Act, not deposited, so an input) or the maximum,
-- whichever is less.
GIVEN `the limit` IS A `Non-economic loss limit`, `the total before the maximum` IS A NUMBER, `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2013 Act total non-economic loss after the s 217 maximum for` `the limit` `on a total of` `the total before the maximum` `in` `the column` MEANS
    min `the total before the maximum` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` (`the 2013 Act s 217 maximum for` `the limit`))

