§§ `MEDICAL AND LIKE SERVICES (CPI) -- ss 224, 229`

-- Lines 675-692: "224(1)(b) Maximum family counselling and therapy and other support services $10,000 $10,310";
-- "224(1)(d) Maximum payment to family members of a severely injured worker who has been immediately hospitalised
-- following the injury for travel and accommodation expenses where the family members residence more than 100km from the
-- hospital $24,850 $25,620"; "224(1)(e) Maximum payment to family members for reasonable travel and accommodation expenses
-- to attend a burial or cremation of a deceased worker if more than 100km from family members residence (These payments
-- came into effect on 27 Sept 2017.) $6,340 $6,540"; "229(4) Contribution to be made by worker towards cost of supported
-- accommodation $45 $46". The rows give no period (per week, per day) for the s 229(4) contribution.
`the 2013 Act s 224(1)(b) maximum` MEANS `printed as` 10000 `then` 10310
`the 2013 Act s 224(1)(d) maximum` MEANS `printed as` 24850 `then` 25620
`the 2013 Act s 224(1)(e) maximum` MEANS `printed as` 6340  `then` 6540
`the 2013 Act s 229(4) contribution` MEANS `printed as` 45 `then` 46

-- The s 224(1)(d) row's own conditions: a severely injured worker, immediately hospitalised following the injury, and the
-- family member's residence more than 100 km from the hospital. Whether a worker is "severely injured" is the Act's
-- (not deposited) and an input.
GIVEN `the worker was severely injured and immediately hospitalised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `kilometres from the family member's residence to the hospital` IS A NUMBER
      `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the 2013 Act s 224(1)(d) maximum where severely injured and hospitalised` `the worker was severely injured and immediately hospitalised` `at` `kilometres from the family member's residence to the hospital` `in` `the column` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the worker was severely injured and immediately hospitalised`)
    THEN `not covered` `the notice prints this travel and accommodation maximum only for the family of a severely injured worker immediately hospitalised after the injury`
    ELSE IF `kilometres from the family member's residence to the hospital` GREATER THAN 100
         THEN `answered` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` `the 2013 Act s 224(1)(d) maximum`)
         ELSE `not covered` `the notice prints this travel and accommodation maximum only where the distance is more than 100 km`

-- The s 224(1)(e) row's own condition: the burial or cremation "more than 100km from family members residence".
-- READING: "more than 100km" is strictly more than 100 km.
GIVEN `kilometres from the family member's residence to the burial or cremation` IS A NUMBER
      `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the 2013 Act s 224(1)(e) maximum for a burial or cremation at` `kilometres from the family member's residence to the burial or cremation` `in` `the column` MEANS
    IF `kilometres from the family member's residence to the burial or cremation` GREATER THAN 100
    THEN `answered` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` `the 2013 Act s 224(1)(e) maximum`)
    ELSE `not covered` `the notice prints this travel and accommodation maximum only where the distance is more than 100 km`

§§ `DISPUTE RESOLUTION (CPI) -- s 301`

-- Lines 410-414: "301(3) Maximum payment for worker's reasonable transportation expenses $77 $79"; "301(4) Maximum payment
-- for worker's loss of income $530 $546". The rows give no unit (per day, per attendance).
DECLARE `Dispute cost` IS ONE OF
    `the worker's reasonable transportation expenses (s 301(3))`
    `the worker's loss of income (s 301(4))`

GIVEN `the cost` IS A `Dispute cost`
GIVETH A `Printed pair`
`the 2013 Act s 301 maximum for` `the cost` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cost`
    WHEN `the worker's reasonable transportation expenses (s 301(3))` THEN `printed as` 77  `then` 79
    WHEN `the worker's loss of income (s 301(4))`                     THEN `printed as` 530 `then` 546

§§ `ACTIONS FOR DAMAGES -- ss 340, 366`

-- Lines 697-706: "Pecuniary Loss (CPI) 340(a)(i) Threshold $77,490 $79,890 / 340(a)(ii) Maximum $1,744,530 $1,798,500 /
-- Pain and Suffering (CPI) 340(b)(i) Threshold $74,820 $77,130 / 340(b)(ii) Maximum $759,510 $783,000 / Damages under
-- Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958 (AWE) 366(2) Death of a person $1,267,530 $1,297,310". What a threshold does (whether
-- damages at or under it are barred, or it is deducted) is in the Act and not encoded.
GIVEN `the head` IS A `Head of damages`, `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH A `Damages figures`
`the 2013 Act s 340 figures for` `the head` `in` `the column` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `pecuniary loss` THEN
        `Damages figures` WITH
            `provision`     IS "s 340(a)"
            `the threshold` IS `the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 77490 `then` 79890)
            `the maximum`   IS `the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 1744530 `then` 1798500)
    WHEN `pain and suffering` THEN
        `Damages figures` WITH
            `provision`     IS "s 340(b)"
            `the threshold` IS `the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 74820 `then` 77130)
            `the maximum`   IS `the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000)

`the 2013 Act s 366(2) amount` MEANS `printed as` 1267530 `then` 1297310
